  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Unified router: live routing traffic, prefix-reuse economics, and failover",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Telemetry from the SCM-supervised router on `127.0.0.1:18101`, scraped under the `fak_router` job (distinct from the generic `fak_gateway` job on `:8080`). This board is the process that emits `fak_router_attempts_total{backend,fallback,status}` alongside the shared `fak_gateway_*` families. **Unavailable means missing evidence**, not zero: an absent series means the router did not report it, not that traffic is idle."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Router health & traffic",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Router scrape (1 = reachable)",
      "description": "Prometheus reachability of the SCM-supervised router listener on :18101. A 0 means the router is up but unreachable to the container, or down; it is the scrape witness, not the router's own readiness.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "up{job=\"fak_router\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "Unavailable",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Total requests",
      "description": "Cumulative HTTP requests the router process has counted on its own `/metrics`. **Read this with *Router attempts* below.** On a routing-mode router every request is admitted and forwarded through the routing path, so the router's own proxy request counter can legitimately read a structural 0 while *Router attempts* climbs into the thousands - the attempt counter, not this one, is the real demand signal there. A monotonic climb here is the single-engine/proxy path; a flat 0 here with a live *Router attempts* row is normal routing mode, **not** an outage (confirm with *Router scrape* = 1). This counter includes all routes, not just chat completions.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 4,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "fak_gateway_requests_total{job=\"fak_router\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "Unavailable",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Streaming requests",
      "description": "Cumulative requests served with streamed responses (SSE). The same routing-mode caveat as *Total requests* applies: a regular request counter that stays at 0 while *Router attempts* advances is the routing path, not a missing scrape. Compare with *Total requests* for the streaming share; a harness that always streams will show the two tracking each other on the single-engine path.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 7
