    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Turn net-win ratio",
      "description": "Most recent completed turn's speedup factor: competitive baseline turn latency divided by the fak turn latency. **0.0 is the un-measured state on a routing-mode router** - the prefix-cache net-win model is only evaluated on the single-engine path, so it stays 0 here rather than being fabricated. **> 1.0 is an operational net win.** This is a last-value gauge, not a rate; pair it with the prefix-reuse row and the routing row.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26,
        "w": 6,
