      "id": 22,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Routing attempts (all backends)",
      "description": "Cumulative upstream attempts the router has made since process start, across every backend and status. **This is the router's real demand signal in routing mode** - read it together with the router's own request counter: a rising attempts row with the request counter at 0 is normal routing (one logical request can fan into several attempts across a fallback chain), not an outage. Unavailable (absent series) means routing mode is off or the scrape failed - missing evidence, never a zero.",
